==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*dumati}}, origin disputed. Either a loan from {{der|ru|gem-pro|*dōmijaną||to judge, think}} (whence {{cog|en|deem}}) either as a direct loan or ultimately from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*dʰewh₂-||to smoke}}, akin to {{cog|sla-pro|*duti||to blow, to inflate}}, {{m|sla-pro|*dymъ||smoke}}. For the latter compare {{m|grc|θῡμός||soul, emotion}}, occasionally also “[[thought]], [[mind]]”. Also compare {{m|ru|надме́нный||supercilious, haughty, arrogant }} as another meaning change to a mental characteristic from the same root.{{rfv-etym|ru}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ду́мать}}
** {{audio|ru|Ru-думать.ogg}}
* {{IPA|ru|[ˈdumat͡sʲ]|a=Belarus}} (''phonetic respelling'': ду́маць)
* {{IPA|ru|[ˈdumɐtʲ]|a=Ukraine}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|ду́мать|impf|pf=поду́мать|vn=ду́мание}}

# to [[think]]
#: {{syn|ru|мы́слить}}
